    sum: "Imperial album and manuscript painting in flat, documentary detail — sieges, processions and city views in bird's-eye.",
    desc: "The palace nakkaşhane (painting studio) produced miniatures for dynastic histories like the Süleymanname: flat-colored, sharply outlined scenes of sieges, ambassador receptions and Istanbul panoramas seen in tilted bird's-eye. Unlike Persian court fantasy, Ottoman miniatures lean documentary — mustered soldiers, real monuments, portraitized sultans — while keeping Persian pattern richness. Artists like Matrakçı Nasuh invented topographic 'road maps' of campaigns. It is a state camera made of brush and pigment.",
