    sum: "Rhythmic scrolling vine-and-leaf ornament that fills any surface with infinite, ordered growth.",
    desc: "Arabesque is the vegetal scroll language of Islamic art: spiraling stems split into half-palmettes and serrated leaves, running in symmetry, layering dense over sparse, and obeying no single center so the eye never rests nor escapes. It carved stucco, wove textiles, glazed tiles and illuminated Qur'ans from Spain to Samarkand. Theoreticians frame it as infinity-suggesting pattern aligned with aniconism, though it predates and exceeds doctrine — it is simply the most adaptable plant that never lived. It pairs with geometric girih grids and calligraphic bands.",
