    sum: "Turned-wood lattice bay windows that cool, veil and ornament the street façades of Islamic cities.",
    desc: "The mashrabiya projects from upper façades as a closed wooden lattice balcony-window: thousands of turnedbalusters in geometric webs admit air and broken light while screening household life from the street, catching night-cooled breezes and passive-cooling rooms with evaporation through the wood. Cairo's historic houses and Damascus courtyards wear tiered rows of them; Gulf towers used them (barjeel windcatchers) alongside. Today parametric designers reinvent mashrabiya as responsive solar screens on desert skyscrapers. Its beauty is climate engineering — shade as lace.",
