    sum: "Living Turkish ceramic-painting tradition continuing İznik's vocabulary — plates, tiles and bowls painted freehand.",
    desc: "Çini names both the craft and its product: fritware painted with cobalt, turquoise and coral-red brushes, then glazed and fired, carried today by Kütahya and İznik workshops. Motifs stay in the classical family — tulips, carnations, birds, hatayi leaves — laid out symmetrically on plates and tiles, and masters sign their brushwork like calligraphers. The Turkish tradition asserts unbroken lineage from the Ottoman kilns, with government-protected Geographical Indication status. It is the bridge between museum İznik and the souvenir plate — with real artistic range between.",
