    desc: "Karagöz plays stage flat cutout puppets of dyed translucent hide jointed at limbs, moved against an oiled white screen by a single puppeteer voicing the whole cast — blustering Karagöz, pompous Hacivat, and the ethnic stereotype stock whose banter satirized Ottoman society. Speech races over a def (tambourine), nakkare and a zurna whistle-trill marking entrances; musical interludes and songs punctuate the farce. Coffeehouse performances were the sitcom of the empire, and Ramadan nights still revive it. Its visual signature: jewel-color translucence and silhouette wit.",
