    sum: "Medieval family watchtowers of rough granite rising beside stone houses — villages built for feud and avalanche.",
    desc: "Upper Svaneti's villages (Chazhashi, Ushguli) cluster medieval koshki towers — four- to five-story stone shafts, base walls a meter thick, entered by ladder-hatch at height — attached to machub family houses of matching rough granite with slate roofs held by stones against mountain wind. Built for vendetta defense, refuge and grain storage, they give the high valleys a skyline of near-identical spires against 5,000-meter peaks. UNESCO inscribed the region; the towers remain in family hands, some still holding their medieval mikvah-like chapel corners.",
